# API layer (`app/api/`)

Extend `Gemvc\Core\ApiService`. Validate and authorize here; **no** business logic or SQL.

URL (Apache): `/api/{Service}/{method}` — convention routing only (no routes file). Bootstrap loads `App\Api\{Service}` and calls the method; catches `AuthException` (401/403) and `RateLimitException` (429).

## Patterns

```php
// Guard whole service (throws AuthException → 401/403)
public function __construct(Request $request) {
    parent::__construct($request);
    $this->requireAuth(['admin']);
    // $this->requireRateLimit(); // optional APCu limit for whole service
}

public function create(): JsonResponse {
    if (!$this->request->definePostSchema([
        'email' => 'email',
        'password' => 'string',
        '?description' => 'string', // optional field
    ])) {
        return $this->request->returnResponse();
    }
    return $this->callController(new UserController($this->request))->create();
}
```

Per-method auth (still valid; returns bool — you must return the response):

```php
if (!$this->request->auth(['admin'])) {
    return Response::unauthorized('Invalid or missing token');
}
```

`auth(['admin'])` / `requireAuth(['admin'])` match against the JWT **`role`** claim (comma-separated role names set when minting tokens, e.g. `$token->role = 'admin,developer'`). Empty `role` fails role checks.

## Rate limits (APCu)

```php
$this->requireRateLimit();              // 20/sec, IP + token; throws → 429
$this->requireRateLimit(5, 'ip', 60);   // 5/sec, IP only, block 60s after exceed
$this->requireRateLimit(10, 'token');   // per JWT
```

Scopes: `both` (default), `ip`, `token`. Fail-open if APCu is missing (requests allowed + warning). Global env: `REQUEST_RATE_LIMIT_PER_SEC`, `REQUEST_RATE_LIMIT_SCOPE`, `REQUEST_RATE_LIMIT_BLOCK_SECONDS`.

Apply on public auth/signup endpoints. If the same write also exists under another service (e.g. `User/create` vs `Auth/register`), rate-limit **both** or clients will bypass.

## Lists

Allowlist GET params before `createList` in the controller:

```php
$this->request->findable(['name' => 'string']);
$this->request->filterable(['role' => 'string']);
$this->request->sortable(['id', 'name', 'created_at']);
```

## Docs PHPDoc

Use `@http`, `@description`, `@example`; `@hidden` to exclude from `/api/Index/document`. Implement `mockResponse(string $method): array` for doc samples.

Schema types: `string`, `int`, `float`, `bool`, `email`, `json`, `decimal`, `uuid`, `slug`, `positive_int`, `timestamp`, …
